From 4894a4c202b252518f9308097525b8312656f2d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:56:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] RomM Library: fix unreadable download and notice screens on
 the device

The infoscreen draws a single line (one TTF_RenderText_Solid call), so every
newline showed as a box and long text ran off the screen.

- Download progress: one line (title cut with "...", progress and hint kept).
- Notices and confirmations: selector menus with the text in the title,
  word-wrapped; confirm is a "No" / "Yes, delete" menu.
- Folder picker returns the folder by item number.
- ui_encoding (latin1|utf8): asked once on first start by showing both
  encodings; redo in Settings > Accents on screen.
- Tests: 159 -> 182 checks (screen_line/screen_wrap widths measured with the
  theme font, calibration, bytes received by the selector).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RhMAqBm84PVkwcVFZvG6f2
